All,
I am trying to create a ggplot2 of cpr and order the factor by calendar month.  I have tried several approaches and none seem to work.  I end up with month in alphabetical order. Below is the code used to make the graph.  I use fct_reorder() to achieve the goal.  A dput of the data is also below.  It seems to me that my approach should have worked.  Any help would be appreciated as I just can't seem to figure out what I am doing wrong.

Thanks,
Glenn

  seasonalfactors %>%
  select(c(month_abb, month_num, loanbalance, cpr)) %>%
  filter(loanbalance == 'LLB') %>%
  ggplot(aes(x = month_abb, y = cpr,
             color = fct_reorder(month_abb, month_num, .fun = mean),
             fill = fct_reorder(month_abb, month_num, .fun = mean))) +
  geom_bar(stat = 'identity') +
  theme_minimal() +
  labs(x = 'Month',
       y = 'CPR',
       caption = 'Source: Bondlab LLC, eMBS',
       title = paste('LLB', 'Seasonal Factors', sep = " ")) +
  scale_colour_tableau(palette = 'Tableau 20') +
  scale_fill_tableau(palette = 'Tableau 20') +
  theme(legend.title = element_blank(),
        legend.position = 'none')
   print(seasonalfactors)

